{"id":10270,"date":"2026-01-09T07:15:26","date_gmt":"2026-01-09T07:15:26","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/?p=10270"},"modified":"2026-01-09T07:15:26","modified_gmt":"2026-01-09T07:15:26","slug":"5-surprising-facts-rodent-pest-control-experts-in-melbourne-want-you-to-know-in-2026","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/5-surprising-facts-rodent-pest-control-experts-in-melbourne-want-you-to-know-in-2026\/","title":{"rendered":"5  Surprising Facts Rodent Pest Control Experts in Melbourne Want You to Know in 2026"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rodent infestations are more common in Melbourne than many people realise, and as urbanisation increases, so does the risk of rodent invasions in homes and businesses.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">While rats and mice may seem like small, manageable pests, their ability to damage property, pose health risks, and create safety hazards makes them a serious problem.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">But many people still hold onto misconceptions about rodents, which often leads to ineffective DIY solutions. Understanding rodent behaviour is key to effective pest control and preventing future infestations.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In this blog, we\u2019ll explore <\/span><b>5 surprising facts<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> about rodents that every Melbourne homeowner should know, especially if you\u2019re facing a rodent issue.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">These insights will help you make informed decisions about pest control and understand why professional help is essential in tackling this problem effectively.<\/span><\/p>\n<h2><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Fact #1: Water Isn\u2019t the Key to Rodent Survival<\/span><\/h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">When it comes to controlling rodent infestations, many homeowners believe that simply cutting off water sources will solve the problem.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The logic is simple: if there\u2019s no water, the rodents will leave, right? Unfortunately, <\/span><b>this is a myth<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Rodents don\u2019t need direct access to water<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to survive. Instead, they can obtain moisture from the food they eat.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This is why, even if you\u2019ve removed all standing water from your home, rodents can still thrive if they have access to food. Whether it\u2019s leftover crumbs, pet food, or pantry items, rodents are adaptable and can survive by getting all the moisture they need from their diet.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Why does this matter for Melbourne homeowners?<\/b><b><br \/>\n<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Simply removing water or using moisture-repelling techniques will not solve the problem. It\u2019s important to <\/span><b>address the real cause of the infestation<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u2014food sources and entry points.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Professional <\/b><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/our-services\/rodent-control-melbourne\/\"><b>rodent pest control in Melbourne<\/b> <\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">focuses on sealing entry points, cleaning food storage areas, and offering solutions that target the root causes of the problem.<\/span><\/p>\n<h2><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Fact #2: Rodents Have Incredible Memory\u2014They\u2019ll Remember Your House<\/span><\/h2>\n<p><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-10272 alignnone\" src=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-01-01-at-5.06.15-PM-300x300.jpeg\" alt=\"Rodent Pest Control Melbourne\" width=\"642\" height=\"642\" srcset=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-01-01-at-5.06.15-PM-300x300.jpeg 300w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-01-01-at-5.06.15-PM-150x150.jpeg 150w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-01-01-at-5.06.15-PM-768x768.jpeg 768w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-01-01-at-5.06.15-PM.jpeg 1024w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 642px) 100vw, 642px\" \/><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Once a rodent enters your home, it doesn\u2019t just leave and forget about it. Rats and mice have <\/span><b>exceptional memory<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, especially when it comes to finding food and shelter.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rodents can <\/span><b>remember their entry routes<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> for years. This means that once a rat or mouse has entered your property, it will likely return again and again, using the same path.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>If you haven\u2019t sealed up the entry points<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, the rodents will simply continue using the same routes to access your home.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Why is this a problem for Melbourne homeowners?<\/b><b><br \/>\n<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rodents don\u2019t just wander into your home at random. They follow a path, and once they\u2019ve found it, they will keep using it unless those entry points are <\/span><b>properly sealed<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This is why many people experience recurring rodent issues. It\u2019s not just about catching the ones you see; you need to prevent them from coming back by ensuring the entry points are blocked off.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>What should you do?<\/b><b><br \/>\n<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The solution is to have a <\/span><b>professional pest control service<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> come in and perform a <\/span><b>thorough inspection<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> of your home. They\u2019ll identify possible entry points and seal any gaps or cracks where rodents could enter.<\/span><\/p>\n<h3><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Fact #3: Rodents Can Cause Fires by Chewing on Wires<\/span><\/h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rodents are known for chewing on just about anything they can find to keep their teeth sharp, and that includes <\/span><b>electrical wires<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. Rodent teeth never stop growing, so they need to constantly gnaw on things to wear them down.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Unfortunately, <\/span><b>electrical wiring is one of their favourite targets<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. This is where the danger lies\u2014when rodents chew through electrical wires, they create <\/span><b>short circuits<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, which can lead to fires. In fact, <\/span><b>many house fires<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> are caused by damaged electrical wiring due to rodent activity.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Why should you care about this in Melbourne?<\/b><b><br \/>\n<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Melbourne homes are often equipped with complex electrical systems, making them especially vulnerable to fire risks caused by rodents. This is an often-overlooked danger, but it\u2019s a serious safety hazard that could result in devastating damage to your home or office.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>How can pest control help?<\/b><b><br \/>\n<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A professional rodent pest control service doesn\u2019t just focus on eliminating the rodents but also addresses <\/span><b>potential safety risks<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. Experts will ensure that rodents don\u2019t damage your electrical wiring and will identify any vulnerable areas that could pose a future risk.<\/span><\/p>\n<h3><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Fact #4: Rodents Reproduce Faster Than Most People Realise<\/span><\/h3>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone  wp-image-10273\" src=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-01-01-at-5.14.16-PM-300x300.jpeg\" alt=\"Rodent Pest Control Melbourne\" width=\"672\" height=\"672\" \/><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">One of the biggest surprises for Melbourne homeowners dealing with a rodent infestation is the <\/span><b>speed at which rodents reproduce<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. If you think you\u2019ve only got one rat or mouse, think again\u2014those two could quickly become <\/span><b>hundreds<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> in the span of a year.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A single pair of rats can produce up to <\/span><b>12 litters per year<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, with each litter containing <\/span><b>up to 12 baby rats<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. That means a single pair can create an entire colony in a matter of months, making a small infestation quickly escalate into a full-blown problem.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Why does this matter for homeowners?<\/b><b><br \/>\n<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The faster you act, the easier it is to prevent the problem from getting out of control. If you wait until the infestation is too large, the damage to your home or business can be significant. <\/span><b>Early rodent pest control<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is critical in stopping this cycle before it becomes unmanageable. The longer you wait, the more difficult and costly the solution will be.<\/span><\/p>\n<h3><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Fact #5: Removing Rodents Alone Won\u2019t Solve the Problem<\/span><\/h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Many people think that once the rats or mice are removed from their home, the job is done. Unfortunately, <\/span><b>this is not the case<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. Even if you remove all the visible rodents, there\u2019s still the matter of <\/span><b>scent marks<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rodents leave behind <\/span><b>urine and scent trails<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to communicate with other rats. These scent trails act as a kind of <\/span><b>&#8220;road map&#8221;<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> for new rodents, attracting them back to the same location. If the scent is not properly cleaned, new rats will continue to follow the trail and enter your home again.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>What\u2019s the solution?<\/b><b><br \/>\n<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To truly solve a rodent problem, you need to <\/span><b>eliminate both the rodents and the scent marks<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> they leave behind. This is where professional rodent pest control comes in. In addition to trapping and removing the rodents, <\/span><b>experts will clean and disinfect the areas<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to remove the scent, and seal off the entry points to prevent further infestations.<\/span><\/p>\n<h4><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Why Clean Homes in Melbourne Still Get Rodents<\/span><\/h4>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone  wp-image-10275\" src=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-01-01-at-5.26.41-PM-300x300.jpg\" alt=\"Rodent Pest Control Melbourne\" width=\"661\" height=\"661\" srcset=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-01-01-at-5.26.41-PM-300x300.jpg 300w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-01-01-at-5.26.41-PM-150x150.jpg 150w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-01-01-at-5.26.41-PM-768x768.jpg 768w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-01-01-at-5.26.41-PM.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 661px) 100vw, 661px\" \/><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It\u2019s a common myth that rodents only infest dirty homes, but this is far from the truth. <\/span><b>Rodents are opportunistic creatures<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> that will invade any home, office, or building where food, warmth, and shelter are available.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Even if your home is spotless, if there\u2019s food exposed or easily accessible, rats and mice will find a way in. <\/span><b>Food storage areas<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, <\/span><b>crumbs in the kitchen<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, and even <\/span><b>pet food<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> can attract rodents, no matter how clean the rest of your home may be.<\/span><\/p>\n<h5><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Why Professional Rodent Pest Control in Melbourne Matters in 2026<\/span><\/h5>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">As Melbourne continues to grow, more construction and development projects are displacing rodents from their natural habitats, pushing them into urban spaces. This makes rodent infestations in homes and businesses a growing concern in the city.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Why is professional pest control important?<\/b><b><br \/>\n<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">While DIY methods may help in the short term, <\/span><b>they don\u2019t offer long-term solutions<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. Professional rodent pest control services focus on a thorough inspection, treatment, and prevention strategy that addresses the full scope of the problem.<\/span><\/p>\n<h6><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rodent Pest Control Is About Prevention, Not Just Removal<\/span><\/h6>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rodents are clever, fast-breeding, and persistent. Understanding their behaviour is essential to getting rid of them for good. It\u2019s not just about catching and removing the rodents\u2014it\u2019s about <\/span><b>preventing them from coming back<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> by sealing entry points, cleaning scent marks, and addressing the root causes of the infestation.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For Melbourne residents, <\/span><b>professional rodent pest control<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is the best way to protect your property and ensure long-term prevention. That\u2019s where <\/span><b>7 States Pest Control<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> comes in.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) About Rodent Pest Control in Melbourne<\/b><\/p>\n<ol>\n<li><b> How can I tell if I have a rodent infestation?<\/b><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Look for droppings, gnaw marks, and scratching noises, especially at night.<\/span><\/p>\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li><b> What should I do if I see a rat or mouse?<\/b><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Contact a professional pest control service for removal and prevention.<\/span><\/p>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li><b> Can I handle a rodent infestation on my own?<\/b><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">DIY methods may not solve the problem long-term. Professional services ensure full removal and prevention.<\/span><\/p>\n<ol start=\"4\">\n<li><b> Why do rodents keep coming back?<\/b><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rodents return if entry points are not sealed or scent trails are not cleaned properly.<\/span><\/p>\n<ol start=\"5\">\n<li><b> How do I prevent rodents from entering my home?<\/b><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Seal cracks, store food properly, and keep your home clean. A pest control service can also help seal entry points.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">With years of experience in Melbourne, <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/\"><b>7 States Pest Control<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> not only removes rodents but also takes the necessary steps to prevent future infestations.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Their team of experts will carry out a thorough inspection of your property, identify potential entry points, and seal them off.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">They use the latest techniques to eliminate existing rodent problems and offer ongoing solutions to keep your home rodent-free for the long term.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>How 7 States Pest Control Handles Rodent Infestations in Melbourne<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At <\/span><b>7 States Pest Control<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, we understand that dealing with a rodent infestation requires more than just eliminating the visible pests.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Our comprehensive approach ensures that the problem is handled at its core, preventing future infestations and providing long-term relief. Here\u2019s how we tackle rodent problems:<\/span><\/p>\n<ol>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Thorough Inspection<\/b><b><br \/>\n<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Our team conducts a detailed inspection of your property to identify signs of rodent activity, entry points, and areas of concern. We check for hidden nests, droppings, and other signs of infestation that may be overlooked.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><\/p>\n<p><\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Sealing Entry Points<\/b><b><br \/>\n<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> We understand that without addressing entry points, rodents will continue to invade. Our experts seal up any cracks or gaps in your home\u2019s foundation, walls, and around windows or doors, ensuring that rodents can no longer enter.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><\/p>\n<p><\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Rodent Trapping and Removal<\/b><b><br \/>\n<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> We use safe and effective trapping methods to remove the existing rodents in your home. Our team ensures that the removal process is thorough and humane, eliminating any risks to your family and pets.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><\/p>\n<p><\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Eliminating Scent Marks<\/b><b><br \/>\n<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Rodents leave scent trails that attract new rodents to your property. Our pest control experts use specialized cleaning techniques to remove these scent marks, making your home less inviting for future rodent activity.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><\/p>\n<p><\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Preventative Measures<\/b><b><br \/>\n<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">After the infestation is resolved, we provide ongoing prevention strategies, including regular inspections and maintenance. We help ensure that your property remains rodent-free and protected from any future invasions.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">By combining expert knowledge with proven methods, <\/span><b>7 States Pest Control<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> provides Melbourne homeowners with a reliable solution to their rodent problems.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/contact-us\/\"><b>Contact 7 States Pest Control Melbourne for expert pest control services that are both safe and reliable.\u00a0<\/b><\/a><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Let our team provide you with a <\/span><b>long-term solution<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> that ensures your home stays rodent-free.<\/span><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Rodent infestations are more common in Melbourne than many people realise, and as urbanisation increases, so does the risk of rodent invasions in homes and businesses.\u00a0 While rats and mice may seem like small, manageable pests, their ability to damage property, pose health risks, and create safety hazards makes them a serious problem. But many [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":10276,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[21],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-10270","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-rodent-pest-control"],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v25.4 - https:\/\/yoast.com\/wordpress\/plugins\/seo\/ -->\n<title>Rodent Pest Control Melbourne: 5 Facts You Need to Know<\/title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Rodent pest control Melbourne: Discover the 5 surprising facts about rodent behavior, fire risks, and why professional control is essential for long-term prevention\" \/>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/5-surprising-facts-rodent-pest-control-experts-in-melbourne-want-you-to-know-in-2026\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Rodent Pest Control Melbourne: 5 Facts You Need to Know\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Rodent pest control Melbourne: Discover the 5 surprising facts about rodent behavior, fire risks, and why professional control is essential for long-term prevention\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/5-surprising-facts-rodent-pest-control-experts-in-melbourne-want-you-to-know-in-2026\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"7 States Pest Control\" \/>\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2026-01-09T07:15:26+00:00\" \/>\n<meta